      ],
      "margin_number": 40,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἐποίησαν Resumption of aorist endings. ἐ- (augment) and -σαν (person-ending).",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 2,
      "bbox": [
        96,
        155,
        128,
        867
      ],
      "margin_number": 42,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ὡς ἔλεγον ‘as I was saying’. Notice the difference between the imperfect tense and the aorists which follow, ‘they made the wax warm etc.’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 3,
      "bbox": [
        191,
        191,
        219,
        270
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Page 65",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 4,
      "bbox": [
        180,
        122,
        230,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": 46,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "If the apparent lack of connection here is confusing, it is designed to convey the ignorance of Strepsiades. ‘Knowing the flea’s leap’ = ‘being educated’, and if he’s educated, then he’s sure to win his lawsuits.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 5,
      "bbox": [
        257,
        191,
        270,
        360
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Translation for 6A",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stage_direction",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        280,
        191,
        295,
        567
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Strepsiades knocks at the door and shouts",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        308,
        89,
        321,
        412
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STREPSIADES",
      "text": "Boy! Young boy!",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        331,
        89,
        345,
        665
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STUDENT",
      "text": "Go to hell. Who knocked at the door? Who shouted?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        351,
        89,
        365,
        483
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STR.",
      "text": "I knocked at the door and I shouted.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        371,
        89,
        386,
        752
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STU.",
      "text": "Who are you that you did that? Some ignoramus, I know well.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 11,
      "bbox": [
        392,
        89,
        406,
        529
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STR.",
      "text": "Strepsiades, from the deme Kikynna.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 12,
      "bbox": [
        412,
        89,
        426,
        351
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STU.",
      "text": "Go to hell, again.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 13,
      "bbox": [
        432,
        89,
        446,
        600
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STR.",
      "text": "Alas! What shall I do? Well, I’ll knock again.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stage_direction",
      "order": 14,
      "bbox": [
        453,
        191,
        467,
        437
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(He knocks at the door again.)",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 15,
      "bbox": [
        474,
        89,
        519,
        903
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STU.",
      "text": "Who’s that knocking? Why did this fellow not stop knocking, when I told him to? Why are you knocking again? What do have in mind? You’ve knocked away my thought [by] doing that.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 16,
      "bbox": [
        525,
        89,
        557,
        900
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STR.",
      "text": "But I’ve just stopped, my dear fellow. For you told me to. Don’t throw me out, although I’m a rustic and ignorant. But what was your thought? Tell me.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 17,
      "bbox": [
        564,
        89,
        578,
        792
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STU.",
      "text": "It isn’t right. Only the students learn these thoughts of the sophists.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 18,
      "bbox": [
        584,
        89,
        598,
        810
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STR.",
      "text": "Tell me then. For I have come to the thinkery as a student of the sophists.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "label": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 19,
      "bbox": [
        604,
        89,
        631,
        831
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STU.",
      "text": "I will tell you. A flea bites Chaerephon’s eyebrow. When it jumps onto Socrates’ head, the men converse as follows.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 20,
      "bbox": [
        638,
        89,
        666,
        856
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "SOCRATES",
      "text": "Look, Chaerephon. The flea does not escape my notice being worthy of an Olympic crown. But tell [me], how many of its own feet did the flea leap?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 21,
      "bbox": [
        673,
        89,
        687,
        827
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "CHAEREPHON",
      "text": "I do not know, Socrates. But why don’t we measure the distance?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 22,
      "bbox": [
        693,
        89,
        707,
        517
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "SOC.",
      "text": "How shall we measure it, Chaerephon?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 23,
      "bbox": [
        713,
        89,
        741,
        903
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "CHA.",
      "text": "Look. First I take some wax, then I make the wax warm. Finally I put the flea’s feet into the wax.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 24,
      "bbox": [
        748,
        89,
        762,
        303
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "SOC.",
      "text": "What then?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 25,
      "bbox": [
        768,
        89,
        782,
        843
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "CHA.",
      "text": "Now the wax is becoming cold. Look, Socrates: for the flea has slippers.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 26,
      "bbox": [
        788,
        89,
        802,
        452
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "SOC.",
      "text": "But what are you doing now?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 27,
      "bbox": [
        808,
        89,
        822,
        490
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "CHA.",
      "text": "Now I am loosing the slippers. Look!",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 28,
      "bbox": [
        828,
        89,
        856,
        903
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STR.",
      "text": "O king Zeus! Oh the wisdom of the men! But tell me, whatever did the men do, student?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 29,
      "bbox": [
        862,
        89,
        907,
        909
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "STU.",
      "text": "You don’t escape my notice being a rustic, Strepsiades, not knowing anything. But as I was saying, first they made the wax warm. Then they put the flea’s feet into the wax. Finally they loosed the slippers and measured – of course – the distance.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    }
  ],
